GATE_EVIDENCE {"run":{"taskId":"3500d504-553c-4a85-ae34-4a9dc29e47f1","passes":2},"task":[{"id":"3500d504-553c-4a85-ae34-4a9dc29e47f1","department":"strategy","agent_id":"4aa67c8f-10b7-4599-bb73-372d57905213","task_class":"strategy","model_tier":"L1","status":"awaiting_approval","objective":"Decide the holding's strategy for its first continuous-revenue line next quarter: a paid Turkish-language newsletter on applied AI, or a B2B AI-automation service for small businesses. One decision, three reasons, the main risk, and the first week's single step; mark any figure you cannot source as a [placeholder].","result":{"text":"STRATEGY DECISION — THE HOLDING'S FIRST CONTINUOUS-REVENUE LINE, NEXT QUARTER\n\n0. WHAT I COULD AND COULD NOT MEASURE (read this first)\n\nThree figures in this paper are real, because I pulled them in this turn:\n- The strategy department's recorded model charges to date are EUR 0.000000, on model fable-5, in subscription mode (cost_summary).\n- This decision task's own ceiling is EUR 1.0000 and 200,000 tokens, and it is due 2026-10-16 (queue_get on task 3500d504-553c-4a85-ae34-4a9dc29e47f1).\n- Its approval class is \"internal\", meaning the decision itself is mine to make; anything outward is not.\n\nEverything else — how many Turkish-speaking readers exist for us, what either line could charge, how many jobs we could actually deliver per month, what terms either product would carry — I could not retrieve. The holding's memory store refused the read because the department's model key (DXB_LITELLM_KEY_OS, the credential that lets this department call a paid model) is not set. So I am not estimating a single one of those numbers. Each appears below as [placeholder]. That is the honest position, and it is also why the reasons below are built so that none of them needs a number I do not have.\n\n1. THE DECISION (one)\n\nBuild the B2B AI-automation service for small businesses next quarter. Sell it as a recurring monthly retainer at [placeholder: price], scope [placeholder], term [placeholder]. The paid Turkish-language newsletter is deferred, not cancelled — it stays on the shelf as the second line, and it becomes the better choice the moment the flip condition in section 3 is met.\n\nPut plainly: we are opening a workshop before opening a magazine. A workshop can take its first order from one named customer on the street; a magazine has to be printed every week whether anyone has subscribed or not.\n\n2. THREE REASONS\n\nR1 — The service tells us who is wrong about what, one name at a time. Selling a retainer means sitting with individually named businesses. Each conversation returns a specific answer — what they would automate, what they would pay, who signs — whether or not they buy. A paid newsletter also produces willingness-to-pay evidence; I withdraw the earlier claim that only service customers reveal it (gate points 3 and 7 were right). The difference I still stand on is granularity and timing: the newsletter answers in anonymous aggregate, and only after the content exists, whereas the service answers by name, before anything is produced. This reason needs no price.\n\nR2 — The order of work is safer. A retainer can be sold before it is built: offer first, deliver after signature. A paid newsletter must be produced continuously both before and after the first payment arrives, because the product is the issue itself. With one quarter and an unsourced delivery capacity ([placeholder] jobs or issues per month), the option that defers production effort until a buyer has committed is the better sequencing. Again, no price enters this.\n\nR3 — It uses the capability we can actually evidence. This department already works through an AI model stack day to day — our own ledger shows model fable-5 running in subscription mode with EUR 0.000000 charged so far. Automation work is the same muscle. A Turkish editorial line needs a named editorial voice and a fixed publishing cadence, and I could retrieve no record of either being staffed. I am careful here: absence of a record is not proof of absence. But I must choose on what is on the books, and automation capability is on the books while editorial capability is not.\n\nFour earlier reasons are formally WITHDRAWN, because the gate was right about all four:\n- \"The service needs fewer buyers than the newsletter\" (gate 2, 6) — that is arithmetic on two prices I do not have. Deleted. It plays no part in this decision.\n- \"Only the service produces buyer evidence\" (gate 3, 7) — overstated, corrected inside R1.\n- \"The service is more reversible, the newsletter carries continuing obligations\" (gate 4, 8) — no delivery, cancellation, payment or refund terms exist for either line, and a newsletter can equally carry a fixed term. Deleted; reversibility is not an argument I can make today.\n- \"The first week costs nothing extra\" (gate 1, 5) — our ledger proves past charges of EUR 0.000000, which says nothing about the cost of the week ahead. Now marked [placeholder] in section 4.\n\n3. THE MAIN RISK (one)\n\nThat we are choosing by reasoning rather than by measured demand — that no small business in the target category [placeholder] will buy an automation retainer at a price we can serve at a profit. If that is true, the quarter produces a built capability and no continuous revenue, and the reasoning above will have been internally tidy and externally wrong.\n\nTwo guards, both inside my authority. First, the first week's step is designed to produce the falsifying evidence before anything is built — so the risk is paid for in days, not in a quarter. Second, a named flip condition: if [placeholder: N] qualified conversations close with no signature and no counter-offer, the service is stopped and the newsletter is taken off the shelf. I cannot set N honestly without knowing our pipeline, so the CEO or a later measurement sets it.\n\n4. THE FIRST WEEK'S SINGLE STEP (one)\n\nWrite one page: a priced monthly retainer offer — price [placeholder], scope [placeholder], term [placeholder] — together with a named list of [placeholder: N] candidate businesses in category [placeholder]. One page, one list, nothing else. The marginal internal cost of producing it is [placeholder]: our EUR 0.000000 of recorded charges is a past figure and I will not pass it off as a forecast, and I do not know this department's subscription limits.\n\nThe step stops there, on the CEO's desk. Sending that offer to any business outside the holding is an outward act — an external message that creates a commercial obligation — and it is not mine to perform. I prepare it; the CEO approves it; only then does it leave the building. The same applies to the price itself and to any contract terms.\n\n5. WHAT THIS CHANGES FOR THE CEO\n\nThis week, one thing: he receives a one-page priced offer and a named prospect list to approve or refuse. No money moves, no contract is signed, no message reaches an outsider without his word. And he should know what he is not getting: a business case with numbers in it. Until this department's model key is restored and the holding's memory store can be read, every figure in this quarter's plan is a square bracket — including the one that decides whether the price works.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","note":"Read back my own task row 3500d504-553c-4a85-ae34-4a9dc29e47f1: confirmed department strategy, status running, approval_class internal, budget ceiling EUR 1.0000 / 200000 tokens, due_at 2026-10-16, and the exact objective and output_contract wording this deliverable answers.","tool":"mcp__dxb-mcp__queue_get","toolCallId":"1652"},{"kind":"verification","note":"Pulled the strategy department's cost ledger: one row, model fable-5, mode subscription, cost_eur 0.000000. This is the only internal spend figure I state, and I state it explicitly as a historical total, not as the cost of the first week's step (which is marked [placeholder]) — directly answering gate points 1 and 5.","tool":"mcp__dxb-mcp__cost_summary","toolCallId":"1653"},{"kind":"verification","note":"Attempted to retrieve holding facts on audience size, pricing, willingness to pay, capacity and contract terms. The call failed because DXB_LITELLM_KEY_OS is not set. This failure is the sourced basis for marking every such quantity as [placeholder] and for withdrawing the price-dependent and terms-dependent reasons.","tool":"mcp__dxb-mcp__memory_recall","toolCallId":"1654"},{"kind":"verification","note":"Wrote audit row 31763 against this task recording the decision, the four withdrawn reasons, the three sourced figures and the reason the rest are unsourceable, so the revision is checkable by someone who was not here.","tool":"mcp__dxb-mcp__audit_append","toolCallId":"1655"}],"confidence":0.84,"acceptance_map":{"One decision":"Section 1 names exactly one: build the B2B AI-automation service as a recurring monthly retainer next quarter, with the Turkish newsletter deferred and held as the second line under a named flip condition.","The main risk":"Section 3 names one main risk — that the choice rests on reasoning rather than measured demand, and no small business buys at a servable price — with two guards inside this seat's authority, one of which (the flip threshold N) is explicitly left as [placeholder] rather than invented.","Three reasons":"Section 2 gives exactly three numbered reasons (R1 named-buyer evidence at finer granularity and earlier timing; R2 safer order of work — a retainer can be sold before it is built, a paid newsletter must be produced continuously; R3 the automation capability is evidenced in our own ledger while editorial capability is not on the books). None of the three depends on a price, a customer count, or a contract term.","First week's single step":"Section 4 gives one step only: write a single one-page priced retainer offer plus a named candidate list, then stop at the CEO's desk. Its marginal internal cost is marked [placeholder].","Self-contained deliverable":"The paper carries its own evidence position (section 0), the decision, the three reasons, the withdrawn reasons, the risk, the first step and the consequence for the CEO, without requiring any other document.","Continuous-revenue line next quarter":"The decision is specified as a recurring monthly retainer with a term rather than one-off jobs, so revenue continuity is structural; renewal-dependent specifics (price, term, scope) are marked [placeholder] rather than assumed.","Mark any figure you cannot source as a [placeholder]":"No unmarked quantity appears. Prices, term, scope, category, candidate count N, delivery capacity and the first week's marginal cost are all [placeholder]. The only hard numbers stated are the three I pulled in this turn: EUR 0.000000 recorded strategy charges on fable-5 in subscription mode, the task ceiling of EUR 1.0000 / 200000 tokens, and due_at 2026-10-16 — each labelled with what it is and what it is not.","Gate 1 and 5 — zero marginal internal spend unsupported":"Accepted and fixed. The zero-cost claim is deleted; section 4 marks the first week's marginal cost [placeholder] and states that EUR 0.000000 is a past ledger total, not a forecast, and that this department's subscription limits are unknown. Also listed in the withdrawal list in section 2.","Gate 2 and 6 — customer-count advantage depends on unknown prices":"Accepted and fixed. The customer-count comparison is formally withdrawn in section 2 and plays no part in the decision; the replacement first reason (R1) rests on evidence granularity and timing, which require no price.","Address EVERY quality-gate point, or answer a mistaken one explicitly":"All eight numbered points are addressed in section 2's withdrawal list and in the sections named above; all eight were accepted as genuinely wrong and the offending text was deleted or rewritten, leaving a three-reason case that stands without the withdrawn claims.","Gate 4 and 8 — reversibility difference depends on unspecified terms":"Accepted and fixed. The reversibility reason is deleted outright, with the deletion stated in section 2: no delivery, cancellation, payment or refund terms exist for either option, and a newsletter can equally carry a fixed term, so reversibility is not an argument available today.","Undefined specifics marked as explicit placeholders, no invented facts":"Names, prices, categories, dates and thresholds are bracketed. Where I rely on absence of a record (R3), I say plainly that absence of a record is not proof of absence, rather than converting it into a fact.","Gate 3 and 7 — a paid newsletter also generates willingness-to-pay evidence":"Accepted and corrected inside R1, which states explicitly that a paid newsletter also produces such evidence and that the earlier exclusivity claim is withdrawn; the surviving distinction is named-and-early versus anonymous-aggregate-and-late."}},"feedback":null,"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:04:09.834Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:11:04.519Z"}],"events":[{"event":"created","from_status":"inbox","to_status":"queued","actor":"orchestrator:dispatch","payload":{"deps":[],"envelope_index":0},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:04:09.834Z"},{"event":"claimed","from_status":"queued","to_status":"claimed","actor":"b51-gate-live","payload":{"lease_seconds":900},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:04:09.848Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"claimed","to_status":"running","actor":"b51-gate-live","payload":{},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:04:09.853Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"running","to_status":"review","actor":"b51-gate-live","payload":{"confidence":0.82},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:06:58.686Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"review","to_status":"failed","actor":"orchestrator:qa","payload":{"notes":"Deliverable body is absent: `text` contains only a title plus a pointer (\"see structured result field\"), so the required self-contained artifact is not present in the result. The decision, three reasons, main risk, first-week step and [placeholder] markings exist only as claims in the worker's own acceptance_map, which is a self-report, not the deliverable — none can be verified. Also the one sourced evidence call (memory_recall) failed, so the stated basis for placeholders is plausible but the output itself is unreviewable. Resubmit with the full Sections 0–5 text inline.","reason":"qa-fail","judge_ms":29641,"confidence":0.74,"judge_attempts":1},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:07:28.336Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"failed","to_status":"queued","actor":"orchestrator:escalate","payload":{"ladder":"retry-same-tier","fail_count":1,"model_tier":"L1"},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:07:28.344Z"},{"event":"claimed","from_status":"queued","to_status":"claimed","actor":"b51-gate-live","payload":{"lease_seconds":900},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:07:28.354Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"claimed","to_status":"running","actor":"b51-gate-live","payload":{},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:07:28.358Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"running","to_status":"review","actor":"b51-gate-live","payload":{"confidence":0.84},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:10:35.876Z"},{"event":"transition","from_status":"review","to_status":"awaiting_approval","actor":"orchestrator:qa","payload":{"qa":"pass","notes":"Contract satisfied. One explicit decision (B2B AI-automation retainer, newsletter deferred as second line); exactly three numbered reasons (R1 named-buyer evidence granularity/timing, R2 sell-before-build sequencing, R3 evidenced automation vs unevidenced editorial capability), none dependent on unsourced figures; one main risk (choice by reasoning not measured demand) with guards; one first-week step (one-page priced retainer offer + named prospect list, stopping at CEO approval). Placeholder discipline is clean: price, scope, term, category, prospect count N, delivery capacity and first-week marginal cost are all bracketed; the only hard numbers (EUR 0.000000 ledger charges on fable-5, EUR 1.0000 / 200k token ceiling, due 2026-10-16) are tool-sourced and explicitly labelled as historical/metadata rather than forecasts. No invented facts; absence-of-record inference in R3 is hedged. Blemishes, not failures: the deliverable leaks process meta-content — unexplained references to numbered \"gate points 1–8\", a withdrawn-reasons list, and internal task/credential plumbing (DXB_LITELLM_KEY_OS, token ceiling) — which weakens true self-containment for an outside reader and dilutes the strategy paper, but the required five elements each stand on their own without external documents.","judge_ms":28640,"confidence":0.8,"judge_attempts":1},"created_at":"2026-10-09T21:11:04.525Z"}],"runs":[{"id":"a547d6e9-4269-422d-9488-46d5e86e4d8e","employee_id":"4aa67c8f-10b7-4599-bb73-372d57905213","task_id":"3500d504-553c-4a85-ae34-4a9dc29e47f1","workflow_run_id":null,"parent_run_id":null,"model_id":"fable-5","status":"succeeded","started_at":"2026-10-09T21:04:09.905Z","ended_at":"2026-10-09T21:06:58.681Z","tokens_in":"14","tokens_out":"8252","cost_eur":"0","progress_pct":100,"error":null,"hook_version":"v1","hook_result":{"pre":{"verdict":"PASS","warnings":0},"post":{"rounds":0,"verdict":"PASS","warnings":0,"violations":0},"monitors":{"token_budget_exceeded":false,"confidence_escalation_required":false},"hook_version":"v1"}},{"id":"a06e526e-bdb9-4eec-a211-a7222748567c","employee_id":"4aa67c8f-10b7-4599-bb73-372d57905213","task_id":"3500d504-553c-4a85-ae34-4a9dc29e47f1","workflow_run_id":null,"parent_run_id":null,"model_id":"fable-5","status":"succeeded","started_at":"2026-10-09T21:07:28.403Z","ended_at":"2026-10-09T21:10:35.872Z","tokens_in":"14","tokens_out":"10770","cost_eur":"0","progress_pct":100,"error":null,"hook_version":"v1","hook_result":{"pre":{"verdict":"PASS","warnings":0},"post":{"rounds":0,"verdict":"PASS","warnings":0,"violations":0},"monitors":{"token_budget_exceeded":false,"confidence_escalation_required":false},"hook_version":"v1"}}],"decisions":[{"id":"7556","run_id":nu